aim and the Petrakos brief) also have a copy under `staging/library/` that is byte-identical\nto the vault copy today. The script and the manual edits change only the vault copies. After\nthey run, the vault is ahead of staging for those files, and any later\n`promote_to_vault.py --apply` over those book folders would overwrite the new links unless\nthe staging copies are refreshed from the vault first.\n\nLink forms: within a book, `[[slug]]`; across books, `[[book/slug]]`, matching what each\nsource file already uses. Exception: the Petrakos brief's two existing links are wrapped in\nbackticks, which stops them rendering as links in Obsidian; its rows follow the plain\n`[[book/slug]]: text` bullet form the Dupuy brief received in the 2026-09-28 wave.\n\nNo library or vault file was edited to produce this list. No git command was run.\n\n---\n\n## strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/\n\n| Source file | Target | Location | Related text to append | Origin |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| supertraining--verkhoshansky/claim--isometric-regional-specificity-not-strictly-angular.md | [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--train-force-at-the-accentuated-joint-angle]] | vault + staging (identical); target vault (promoted 2026-10-03) | [[heuristic--train-force-at-the-accentuated-joint-angle]] (4.3.2, choosing an isometric training angle from where the sport action peaks; that entry cites this one's spread of about 15 degrees either side as a limit on strict angle matching) | Writer's list |\n36:## strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/\n51:## strength-and-conditioning/block-periodization--issurin/\n57:## strength-and-conditioning/fundamentals-of-sprinting--moyer/\n64:## research-papers/\n73:## Dropped suggestions (found, but excluded), with reason\n82:## Manual edits (not handled by the script)\n   Old:\n   \"culminated\" in Verkhoshansky's principle of dynamic correspondence (see 4.3). On this\n   New:\n   \"culminated\" in Verkhoshansky's 