{"parentUuid":"86d9edbf-0ccb-4628-8f52-a6bcd857f888","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"bb7640f3-4c73-49eb-8121-41eedd8509ec","agentId":"a8e36db408996cf67","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JYgQN4Qtpuaq7bWhh7YCUh","type":"tool_result","content":"## strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/\n\n| Source file | Target | Location | Related text to append | Origin |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| supertraining--verkhoshansky/claim--isometric-regional-specificity-not-strictly-angular.md | [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--train-force-at-the-accentuated-joint-angle]] | vault + staging (identical); target vault (promoted 2026-10-03) | [[heuristic--train-force-at-the-accentuated-joint-angle]] (4.3.2, choosing an isometric training angle from where the sport action peaks; that entry cites this one's spread of about 15 degrees either side as a limit on strict angle matching) | Writer's list |\n| supertraining--verkhoshansky/claim--joint-angle-specific-strength-training-narrows-transfer.md | [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--train-force-at-the-accentuated-joint-angle]] | vault + staging (identical); target vault (promoted 2026-10-03) | [[heuristic--train-force-at-the-accentuated-joint-angle]] (4.3.2, the rule to train force at the joint angle where the sport action peaks; that entry cites this claim as a qualifier, since training at a shortened angle transfers less across the range) | Writer's list |\n| supertraining--verkhoshansky/claim--joint-angle-and-limb-position-changes-force-output.md | [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--match-amplitude-direction-and-line-of-resistance-to-the-sport]] | vault + staging (identical); target vault (promoted 2026-10-03) | [[heuristic--match-amplitude-direction-and-line-of-resistance-to-the-sport]] (4.3.1, where the same 210° hip angle is used to argue that a standing hip-flexor machine misses the sprinter's range) | Writer's list |\n| supertraining--verkhoshansky/framework--r