 Source file | Target | Location | Related text to append | Origin |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| research-papers/petrakos-2016-resisted-sled-sprint-training-to-improve-sprint-performance-a-systematic-review.md | [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/claim--parachute-resistance-tradeoffs-for-dynamic-correspondence]] | vault (paper brief; added as a bullet under \"## Related knowledge\"); target vault (promoted 2026-10-03) | [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/claim--parachute-resistance-tradeoffs-for-dynamic-correspondence]]: Supertraining 4.3.1 argues parachutes are safer than a dragged sled because they add no vertical reaction force, a claim this review's performance data do not test | Writer's list |\n| research-papers/petrakos-2016-resisted-sled-sprint-training-to-improve-sprint-performance-a-systematic-review.md | [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--parachute-resistance-sizing-progression-and-contrast-release]] | vault (paper brief; added as a bullet under \"## Related knowledge\"); target vault (promoted 2026-10-03) | [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--parachute-resistance-sizing-progression-and-contrast-release]]: Supertraining 4.3.1 sizes parachutes by speed quality (small for speed, large for acceleration-strength) from practice, not trials; this review likewise could not define an optimal sled load | Writer's list |\n\n---\n\n## Dropped suggestions (found, but excluded), with reason\n\nNone dropped. Four writer suggestions are not script rows because they replace existing text\nrather than append to Related; they are listed under Manual edits:\n\n- **`principle--specificity-of-training-ten-dimensions` -> five-criteria entry**: replaces the \"not yet ingested\" placeholder in the body.\n- **`heuristic--isokinetic-testing-limitations-for-functional-sport-specificity` and `heuristic--choice-of-muscle-training-regime-favor-combination` -> five-criteria entry**: extend an inline \"(see 4.3)\".\n- **Evans `case-study--dynamic-correspondence-applied-to-wrestling-takedown` -> five-criteria entry and boxer/shot-putter entry**: its Related paragraph is a reciprocal-link placeholder, not a link list, and it is followed directly by a stray `</content>` line. The script's `add()` extends the Related paragraph until a blank line or a line starting with `**`; `</content>` is neither, so an append would land after `</content>` and leave the stale placeholder in place. Same routing as the 2026-09-28 natural-asymmetry placeholder.\n\n## Manual edits (not handled by the script)\n\nMake these in the vault (`/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/`). The four\nfiles below are not sources of any script row, so order does not matter. Each Old string was\nconfirmed to occur exactly once in its file. The staging copies under `staging/library/` are\nidentical to the vault today; edit them too, or refresh them from the vault, before any later\npromotion of these folders.\n\n1. **`strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/principle--specificity-of-training-ten-dimensions.md`**, line 49 (When to apply, inside the **Inference:** sentence). Source: writer's list; review_supertraining_ch4-3-4_opus.md, \"Duplicates\".\n\"\"\"Append reciprocal Related links from a staging/reciprocal_links_*.md table to vault files.\n\n    python scripts/apply_reciprocal_links.py staging/reciprocal_links_2026-09-27.md           # dry run\n    python scripts/apply_reciprocal_links.py staging/reciprocal_links_2026-09-27.md --apply\n\nRun AFTER promote_to_vault.py --apply, so every source file is in the vault. Table rows:\n| source (path under Knowledge/library, domain optional) | [[target]] | location | text | origin |\nLibrary entries: the text is added as a new line at the end of the **Related** paragraph, or\na **Related** paragraph is created at the end of the file. Paper briefs: added as a bullet\nunder \"## Related knowledge\" (replacing a \"None identified\" placeholder). A row is skipped\nwhen the source already links the target.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nVAULT = Path(r\"/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library\")\n\n\ndef resolve(src: str) -> Path | None:\n    src = src.strip().strip(\"`\")\n    hits = [p for p in VAULT.rglob(\"*.md\") if p.as_posix().endswith(\"/\" + src)]\n    return hits[0] if len(hits) == 1 else None\n\n\ndef add(text: str, line: str) -> str:\n    lines = text.rstrip(\"\\n\").split(\"\\n\")\n    if \"## Related knowledge\" in text:\n        i = next(k for k, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith(\"## Related knowledge\"))\n        j = i + 1\n        while j < len(lines) and not lines[j].startswith(\"## \"):\n            j += 1\n        block = [l for l in lines[i + 1:j] if l.strip() and \"None identified\" not in l]\n        if block and not block[-1].startswith(\"- \"):\n            block.append(\"\")\n        return \"\\n\".join(lines[:i + 1] + [\"\"] + block + [f\"- {line}\", \"\"] + lines[j:]).rstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\"\n    rel = [k for k, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith(\"**Related**\")]\n    if rel:\n        j = rel[-1] + 1\n        while j < len(lines) and lines[j].strip() and not lines[j].startswith(\"**\"):\n            j += 1\n        lines[j - 1] = lines[j - 1].rstrip().rstrip(\".;\") + \"; \" + line\n        return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\"\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines + [\"\", f\"**Related** — {line}\"]) + \"\\n\"\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"table\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--apply\", action=\"store_true\")\n    a = ap.parse_args()\n    rows = [r for r in Path(a.table).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").split(\"\\n## Dropped\")[0].splitlines()\n            if r.startswith(\"| \") and \"[[\" in r]\n    done = skipped = failed = 0\n    for r in rows:\n        cells = [c.strip() for c in r.strip().strip(\"|\").split(\"|\")]\n        src, target, text = cells[0], cells[1], cells[3]\n        slug = re.search(r\"\\[\\[([^\\]|]+)\", target).group(1).split(\"/\")[-1]\n        path = resolve(src)\n        if path is None:\n            failed += 1\n            print(f\"UNRESOLVED source: {src}\")\n            continue\n        body = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        if re.search(r\"\\[\\[[^\\]]*\" + re.escape(slug) + r\"[\\]|#]\", body):\n            skipped += 1\n            continue\n        done += 1\n        print(f\"{'ADD' if a.apply else 'would add'}: {path.relative_to(VAULT).as_posix()} -> {slug}\")\n        if a.apply:\n            path.write_text(add(body, text), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    print(f\"\\n{done} {'added' if a.apply else 'to add'}, {skipped} already linked, {failed} unresolved\")\n    return 1 if failed else 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\nclaim--newton-ii-and-impulse-momentum-as-the-math-behind-the-force-time-curve.md\nprinciple--speed-strength-strength-endurance-and-speed-endurance-are-independent-qualities.md\nheuristic--analytical-synthetic-and-multifaceted-preparation-suit-only-early-training.md\nheuristic--dynamic-correspondence-means-matching-motor-characteristics-not-copying-the-sport-movement.md\nframework--special-strength-methods-classified-by-sport-group-and-strength-type.md\nframework--three-methods-for-maximum-strength-repetitive-brief-maximal-isometric.md\nclaim--delorme-oxford-mccloy-progressive-resistance-variants-compared.md\nclaim--berger-sets-reps-and-frequency-studies-in-novices.md\nclaim--moderate-and-mixed-movement-tempo-for-repetition-strength-gains.md\nclaim--ivanov-1966-contraction-mode-and-which-strength-test-improves.md\nframework--apre-autoregulating-progressive-resistance-exercise.md\nheuristic--apre-skill-learning-6rm-pyramid-test-and-rm-muscle-testing.md\nheuristic--isometric-apre-six-second-maximum-protocol.md\nframework--two-groups-of-speed-strength-movements-and-their-tension-types.md\nheuristic--speed-strength-loading-light-loads-maximal-acceleration-and-5-to-1-mix.md\nclaim--implement-mass-for-speed-strength-keep-technique-an