{"parentUuid":"cd41dd5a-c2d5-4f55-bae6-0fd44b656b36","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"bb7640f3-4c73-49eb-8121-41eedd8509ec","agentId":"a8e36db408996cf67","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018KKK5xrfepSgbgsYBTn13q","type":"tool_result","content":"fixes_supertraining_ch5a_applied.md\nfixes_supertraining_ch5b_applied.md\nfixes_supertraining_ch5c_applied.md\nreview_supertraining_ch5a_opus_round2.md\nreview_supertraining_ch5a_opus.md\nreview_supertraining_ch5b_opus_round2.md\nreview_supertraining_ch5b_opus.md\nreview_supertraining_ch5c_opus_round2.md\nreview_supertraining_ch5c_opus.md\n      58 review_supertraining_ch5a_opus_round2.md\n      62 review_supertraining_ch5a_opus.md\n      87 review_supertraining_ch5b_opus_round2.md\n      86 review_supertraining_ch5b_opus.md\n      76 review_supertraining_ch5c_opus_round2.md\n      76 review_supertraining_ch5c_opus.md\n     113 fixes_supertraining_ch5a_applied.md\n     147 fixes_supertraining_ch5b_applied.md\n     125 fixes_supertraining_ch5c_applied.md\n     830 total\nreview_supertraining_ch5a_opus.md:7:Links: every `[[wikilink]]` in the 19 files resolves to a file in the vault library or the staging library. Claims the entries make about linked entries were spot-checked (Bischke & Morehouse in the PAP entry; breath-holding in the isometric drawbacks entry; Moyer wearable-resistance entry \"wrong in three separate ways\"; Bondarchuk leg-to-leg 50 m \"all levels\"; \nreview_supertraining_ch5a_opus.md:8:Duplicates: searched the vault library and all staging libraries (including the 5b and 5c files in the same folder) for impulse-momentum, DeLorme, APRE/DAPRE, Berger, Ivanov 1966, Lelikov, analytical-synthetic, cross training, multi-faceted, Rogener, Egstrom, Zubov, thigh cuffs, Table 5.3, Krusen, Narikashvili, 6SM, \"20% of 1RM\", \"independent qualities\", \"litera\nreview_supertraining_ch5a_opus.md:17:| principle--speed-strength-strength-endurance-and-speed-endurance-are-independent-qualities.md | GO | none | checked: \"totally independent qualities\", \"does not necessarily enhance\", \"(Verkhoshansky, 1963)\", \"inversely proportional to one another (see Ch 4)\" at PDF 268 / p.257 (image); Example labelled Inference; baseline line 101 quote and Explicit Q1 tag; `s\nreview_supertraining_ch5a_opus.md:18:| heuristic--analytical-synthetic-and-multifaceted-preparation-suit-only-early-training.md | GO | none | checked: analytical-synthetic definition, gymnasts/weightlifters sprints and barbell for track (Verkhoshansky 1977), \"appropriate only for the initial stages ... serious error for highly-qualified athletes to use them casually\", \"partly true and only under c\nreview_supertraining_ch5a_opus.md:43:## Reciprocal-link suggestions\nreview_supertraining_ch5c_opus.md:43:Reciprocal links to add (not blocking): novice case and sequence heuristic to `claim--depth-jump-training-beat-higher-volume-traditional-training-in-jumpers`; restoration heuristic to `claim--delayed-strength-training-effect-lag-before-gains-appear`.\nreview_supertraining_ch5b_opus_round2.md:79:- `case-study--novice-strength-and-speed-strength-sequencing-experiments.md` (5c) already links back to the 475-jumps entry. It does not link to `heuristic--brief-maximal-tension-vs-plyometrics-by-resistance-size`, which now cites it. Add that reciprocal link.\nreview_supertraining_ch5b_opus.md:62:No duplicates found. I checked the vault supertraining folder, the staging folder (including batches 5a and 5c) and the vault research papers for depth jump, plyometric, strength-endurance, Lewis, inertia and state-dependent. The overlaps already link to the earlier entries: Ch1 shock-method terminology, Ch1.7 fibre-type prescription, Ch4.2.3 optimal drop heigh\nfixes_supertraining_ch5c_applied.md:42:Optional items from the review (not required, not done): the two reciprocal links into `claim--depth-jump-training-beat-higher-volume-traditional-training-in-jumpers` and `claim--delayed-strength-training-effect-lag-before-gains-appear` point into 5a / 4.1 files, which are outside my scope. Missing idea 2 (individualising one circuit by contraction type, post\nfixes_supertraining_ch5c_applied.md:123:2. Back-link added in `case-study--novice-strength-and-speed-strength-sequencing-experiments.md` Related to `heuristic--brief-maximal-tension-vs-plyometrics-by-resistance-size` (suggested by the 5b round-2 review).\nfixes_supertraining_ch5a_applied.md:109:For the promoter: confidence tallies are unchanged. The Newton entry stays `proven`, scoped to the identity. The two renamed entries keep `supported`. The review's optional reciprocal-link suggestions were not applied, because they touch GO entries and 5b/5c files outside this fix scope.\nfixes_supertraining_ch5b_applied.md:54:- Reciprocal links (5c, not edited by me): `case-study--novice-strength-and-speed-strength-sequencing-experiments.md` should link back to [[claim--depth-jump-training-beat-higher-volume-traditional-training-in-jumpers]] and [[heuristic--brief-maximal-tension-vs-plyometrics-by-resistance-size]].","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7f32fb1d-3edc-4fb6-bf96-b81e8f2de7b7","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:01:42.401Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"fixes_supertraining_ch5a_applied.md\nfixes_supertraining_ch5b_applied.md\nfixes_supertraining_ch5c_applied.md\nreview_supertraining_ch5a_opus_round2.md\nreview_supertraining_ch5a_opus.md\nreview_supertraining_ch5b_opus_round2.md\nreview_supertraining_ch5b_opus.md\nreview_supertraining_ch5c_opus_round2.md\nreview_supertraining_ch5c_opus.md\n      58 review_supertraining_ch5a_opus_round2.md\n      62 review_supertraining_ch5a_opus.md\n      87 review_supertraining_ch5b_opus_round2.md\n      86 review_supertraining_ch5b_opus.md\n      76 review_supertraining_ch5c_opus_round2.md\n      76 review_supertraining_ch5c_opus.md\n     113 fixes_supertraining_ch5a_applied.md\n     147 fixes_supertraining_ch5b_applied.md\n     125 fixes_supertraining_ch5c_applied.md\n     830 total\nreview