{"parentUuid":"b8ebff3b-2d95-46cf-b030-5f9f47e0ab6a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f3859be2-3513-4b8e-bb88-ac5e3cefe2da","agentId":"a8e36db408996cf67","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LTBPewWaViQfhot1V3hhSf","type":"tool_result","content":"enhancing-skill--myszka/principle--specifying-vs-non-specifying-information.md:0\nenhancing-skill--myszka/principle--task-simplification-not-decomposition.md:0\nenhancing-skill--myszka/principle--variability-overuse-hypothesis.md:0\nenhancing-skill--myszka/framework--direct-learning-attention-intention-calibration.md:1\nenhancing-skill--myszka/framework--newell-interacting-constraints.md:1\n   2 [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--instruction-type-and-verbal-framing-shape-strength-output]]\n   1 [[enhancing-skill--myszka/_book|Enhancing Skill in American Football: Revolutionizing Practice Design for Transfer to Game Day]]\n   1 [[../strength-and-conditioning/_domain|strength-and-conditioning]]\n**When to apply** — Youth and off-season programming, and cross-training conversations where \"any activity is good activity\" is the default. It also gives a defensible answer to a parent asking whether their child should specialise: the framework says variety is not a distraction from development, i\n\n**When NOT to apply** — Marked **untested**, and the authors say why in their own words: **\"these ideas still remain to be thoroughly tested in research studies\"** and parkour transfer holds only **\"in theory.\"** Every mechanism here is plausible and unproven for football specifically. Donor sports \n\n**Example** — Use the three tests. Basketball: shared affordances (space, gaps, opponents), shared information (interpersonal distance, closing rates), exploratory structure. Passes. A prescribed agility class with a set sequence: fails the third test, whatever it does for fitness.\n**Related** — [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--instruction-type-and-verbal-framing-shape-strength-output]]: tension - direct-learning/attention-intention calibration favors constraint manipul\n**Related** — [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--instruction-type-and-verbal-framing-shape-strength-output]]: tension - Harries/Supertraining's \"concrete\" verbal-cue instruction type is the pre","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"735ba405-9d1f-449c-a070-489d70fc3018","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:06:06.316Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"enhancing-skill--myszka/principle--specifying-vs-non-specifying-information.md:0\nenhancing-skill--myszka/principle--task-simplification-not-decomposition.md:0\nenhancing-skill--myszka/principle--variability-overuse-hypothesis.md:0\nenhancing-skill--myszka/framework--direct-learning-attention-intention-calibration.md:1\nenhancing-skill--myszka/framework--newell-interacting-constraints.md:1\n   2 [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--instruction-type-and-verbal-framing-shape-strength-output]]\n   1 [[enhancing-skill--myszka/_book|Enhancing Skill in American Football: Revolutionizing Practice Design for Transfer to Game Day]]\n   1 [[../strength-and-conditioning/_domain|strength-and-conditioning]]\n**When to apply** — Youth and off-season programming, and cross-training conversations where \"any activity is good activity\" is the default. It also gives a defensible answer to a parent asking whether their child should specialise: the framework says variety is not a distraction from development, i\n\n**When NOT to apply** — Marked **untested**, and the authors say why in their own words: **\"these ideas still remain to be thoroughly tested in research studies\"** and parkour transfer holds only **\"in theory.\"** Every mechanism here is plausible and unproven for football specifically. Donor sports \n\n**Example** — Use the three tests. Basketball: shared affordances (space, gaps, opponents), shared information (interpersonal distance, closing rates), exploratory structure. Passes. A prescribed agility class with a set sequence: fails the third t