s and phase; it cites this entry for the contralateral \"cross-training\" effect, a different use of the term) | 5c writer's Ch1-4 sources |\n| supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--parachute-resistance-sizing-progression-and-contrast-release.md | [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--strength-endurance-under-demanding-sport-like-conditions]] | vault + staging (identical); target vault (promoted 2026-10-03) | [[heuristic--strength-endurance-under-demanding-sport-like-conditions]] (5.2.5, strength-endurance under demanding but sport-like conditions, such as a runner with a small parachute or a loaded sled, Popov 1966) | 5c writer's Ch1-4 sources |\n| supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--parachute-resistance-sizing-progression-and-contrast-release.md | [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/framework--circuit-layout-variants-superset-retrophase-zigzag-detour]] | vault + staging (identical); appends after the previous row; target vault (promoted 2026-10-03) | [[framework--circuit-layout-variants-superset-retrophase-zigzag-detour]] (5.6, circuit layouts; its water stations rest on the same velocity-squared resistance relation given here for parachute drag) | 5c writer's Ch1-4 sources |\n| supertraining--verkhoshansky/claim--delayed-strength-training-effect-lag-before-gains-appear.md | [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next]] | vault + staging (identical); target vault (promoted 2026-10-03) | [[heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next]] (5.3.3, a restorative period after a concentrated block, with gains after a 1-3 week latency; it cites this entry's 18-25% speed-strength rise after a 10-day rest as an in-library case for a short latency; rated contested) | review_supertraining_ch5c_opus.md, \"Duplicates\"; fixes_supertraining_ch5c_applied.md (optional item not done) |\n| supertraining--verkhoshansky/framework--four-mechanisms-of-stimulating-muscular-tension.md | [[supertraini