ors' warning against literally copying the sport movement under load; select means that match its key motor characteristics instead) | Writer's list (5a) |\n\n## strength-and-conditioning/fundamentals-of-sprinting--moyer/\n\n| Source file | Target | Location | Related text to append | Origin |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| fundamentals-of-sprinting--moyer/claim--wearable-resistance-kinetic-energy-sprint.md | [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/case-study--alternate-leg-bounding-with-thigh-cuffs-for-sprinters]] | vault only (no staging copy); target vault (promoted 2026-10-03) | [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/case-study--alternate-leg-bounding-with-thigh-cuffs-for-sprinters]] (Supertraining 5.2.3, Verkhoshansky's sprinters bounding with 100-150 g cuffs on each thigh, an earlier light thigh load given without data; that entry notes this entry's kinetic-energy findings do not support the cuffs) | Writer's list (5a) |\n\n## skill-acquisition/enhancing-skill--myszka/\n\n| Source file | Target | Location | Related text to append | Origin |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| enhancing-skill--myszka/framework--choosing-a-donor-sport.md | [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--choose-cross-training-by-fitness-qualities-and-phase-not-sport-label]] | vault only (no staging copy); the file has no **Related** paragraph (it ends on Example), so the script creates one; target vault (promoted 2026-10-03) | [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--choose-cross-training-by-fitness-qualities-and-phase-not-sport-label]]: Supertraining 5.5 chooses cross-training activities by the fitness qualities and training phase they serve, not the sport label; a fitness-based angle on the same donor-sport question | Writer's list (5c) |\n\n## research-papers/\n\n| Source file | Target | Location | Related text to append | Origin |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| research-papers/issurin-2016-benefits-and-limitations-of-block-periodized-training-approaches-to-athletes-preparation-a.md | [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/fr