to the end of the meeting notes. Handled as Manual edit 3 (on the \"Daily monitoring\" bullet).\n- **Ch2.3.1 placeholder in `claim--physical-quality-transfer-decreases-as-specific-fitness-increases`, line 65** (\"defer that judgment to later chapters not yet ingested\"): not edited. The book's own sentence (PDF p. 128, printed p. 117) says only that the complex-training claim \"is examined later in this and later chapters\", without naming a section, and Chapters 6-8 are still not ingested, so \"not yet ingested\" stays true. The two 5.1 entries that take up the question are linked from this file by the script rows above.\n\n## Manual edits (not handled by the script)\n\nMake these in the vault (`/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/`). None of the three\nfiles is the source of a script row except file 1 (the isokinetic heuristic, which also gets the\nAPRE testing-heuristic row); that edit touches a body sentence, not the Related paragraph, so\norder does not matter. Each Old string was confirmed to occur exactly once in its file. The\nisokinetic heuristic's staging copy under `staging/library/` is identical to the vault today; edit\nit too, or refresh it from the vault, before any later promotion of that folder. Files 2 and 3\nhave no staging copy.\n\n1. **`strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--isokinetic-testing-limitations-for-functional-sport-specificity.md`**, line 62 (end of What it is). Source: writer's list (5a).\n\n   ```\n   Old:\n   authors also name the APRE system (based on DeLorme's original work, see 5.2.2) as an\n   New:\n   authors also name the APRE system (based on DeLorme's original work, see 5.2.2, [[framework--apre-autoregulating-progressive-resistance-exercise]]) as an\n   ```\n\n2. **`strength-and-conditioning/fundamentals-of-sprinting--moyer/framework--isometric-set-positions-ankle-knee-hip.md`**, line 36 (last line of the file, the dated bullet under **Related**): add a second dated bullet after it, in the same form. The file should still end with a single newline. Source: writer's list (5a).\n\n   ```\n   Old:\n   - Added 2026-09-26: [[heuristic--75-85-percent-mv-decision-gate]]: an RTP application of isometric force benchmarks (Nordic and seated calf) as a gate before faster running.\n   New:\n   - Added 2026-09-26: [[heuristic--75-85-percent-mv-decision-gate]]: an RTP application of isometric force benchmarks (Nordic and seated calf) as a gate before faster running.\n   - Added 2026-10-03: [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--isometric-apre-six-second-maximum-protocol]]: Supertraining 5.2.2's isometric APRE, 6-second maximal holds at a set joint angle with 5-10 s rest, set 1 at 50% and set 2 at 75% of the 6SM weight; a load progression for isometric stations like these.\n   ```\n\n3. **`strength-and-conditioning/velocity-based-training-implementation-guide-from-texas-am.md`**, line 27 (the \"Daily monitoring\" bullet under \"## Key topics\"). The APRE entry already links this note (\"daily autoregulation by bar velocity\"). Source: writer's list (5a).\n\n   ```\n   Old:\n   - **Daily monitoring**: Velocity autoregulation fosters responsiveness to individual readiness levels\n   New:\n   - **Daily monitoring**: Velocity autoregulation fosters responsiveness to individual readiness levels (a rep-based counterpart: [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/framework--apre-autoregulating-progressive-resistance-exercise]], Supertraining 5.2.2's APRE, which sets the next load from the reps achieved)\n   ```\n\n---\n\n**Counts:** 68 script rows (supertraining 41, issurin 8, bompa 2, bondarchuk 4, zatsiorsky 3,\nevans 1, moyer 1, myszka 1, research-papers 1, in-batch 6). Manual edits 3. Dropped 8 (one\nalready linked; two writer readings the files do not support; four in-batch links already\napplied by the fixers, listed as one item; three routed to Manual edits; one placeholder left\nas is).\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfffxTE4V2QLURid9izxb","attributionAg